  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a witness whose effect closure reaches gunbc.host.host_effect_realize -> ... -> gunbc.fleet.fleet_known_hosts_anchor.portable_remote_words refuses to resolve at all, with the single refusal 'effect summary incomplete: call to skip in gunbc.fleet.fleet_known_hosts_anchor.portable_remote_words has no established callee identity, so its effects cannot be joined' at dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_known_hosts_anchor.dag:767:86, while the rest of the file resolves clean. HARM: execution evidence is blocked for every live_deploy / host / fleet control whose closure reaches host_effect_realize, because the whole entry refuses at the resolve stage rather than reporting a per-item effect. SPECIMEN: dag/test/claim/host/approval_broker_tree_install_witness.dag an_unbound_revision_refuses_before_any_observation, reproducing verbatim on main cb8b6693 (and on the seed build of da9e9f5); the bare call is skip(xs: ws, n: 1) at fleet_known_hosts_anchor.dag:767, whose target is std.algebra.skip (dag/std/algebra.dag:1364), imported by the listed import 'import std.algebra { trim, list_head, skip }'. DISTINGUISHING FACT: in the SAME function, the line above (list_head(xs: ws)) resolves while skip(xs: ws, n: 1) does not, though both are imported identically from std.algebra and both are generic over FreeMonoid called with a List argument; the only difference is that skip is ALSO an algebra method template name (the kernel_algebra_profile free_monoid_collection template 'skip', dispatched as xs.skip(n:)) while list_head is not. Under the namespace-only name-resolution policy the effect-summary func env carries none of the module's listed imports (measured on the failing call: func_env_declared_func_sig=Unresolved over 129 func_env parents with skip declared by none of them), so a bare call to an imported free function is answered ONLY by the census authorities census_declaration_identity / func_sig_from_global_bare, and both blanket-bailed on algebra_method_template_name -- a gate added so a receiver-dispatched bare map/join reaches the known-method bridge instead of a bogus census declaration. A listed-imported free function whose spelling collides with a method template therefore reached no callee authority at all, and the effect join classified it UnresolvedCallee. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, found while unblocking execution evidence for the warm-ibex-158 deploy-artifact gate (#16546/#16550). REPAIR NOT TAKEN HERE: none -- the repair was taken: each census gate yields on the method-template spelling exactly when import_visible_name(env, name) is true, so a genuine listed import is bound to its declaration while a non-imported method-template name (map/join) still yields to the method bridge, preserving the regression the gate was added for. CONTROLS: an_unbound_revision_refuses_before_any_observation (red on main, green on the head), the same witness's parse_rebases_absolute_paths_onto_the_subdirectory (green on both, it does not reach the call), and the real-route host / live_deploy controls that reach host_effect_realize. CEILING: mechanically preventable inside the seed resolver for the listed-import case, which is now bound; the routing of NON-imported method-template bare names to the method bridge is a deliberate external design boundary, not a defect. NEXT TRIGGER: the effect-summary env should carry the module's listed imports so that callee identity never depends on the census fallback, and the gate-versus-import interaction cannot diverge between the normal resolve pass (which saw std.algebra in 194 parents and resolved) and the effect-summary pass (which did not).",
      "CURRENT RUNG (2026-11-23, main 4a63370f4a67, released claim_batch run 45059586538, srv1): MITIGATABLE (the class is repaired and measured, but one manual run blocks nothing). Executed controls, all via claim_batch over dag/test/claim/effect_summary_listed_import: a listed import of an effectful declaration whose name two modules declare resolves (PASS listed_import_binds_the_effectful_declaration); a listed std.algebra method-template name resolves (PASS bare_method_template_name_binds_through_the_listed_import); a listed generic free fn resolves (PASS generic_free_fn_binds_through_the_listed_import); the same bare call with the import UNLISTED still refuses 'effect summary incomplete ... no established callee identity' (a scratch control, deliberately NOT committed because a committed claim witness must never fail by design; its raw run is in the PR body), so no module-wide ancestry binds it; an_unbound_revision_refuses_before_any_observation PASS. The witnesses are not on the required gate and no CI job executes them, so the rung stays mitigatable until a required_gate_authored_modules row (operator ruling) enrols them; the unlisted control is not committed; a refusal-asserting PASSING witness for it is the next-rung work. NOT SHOWN: that the census fallback is removable; the inference env already carries listed imports (build_module_context -> func_env_views_for_import), the census answers only on a func-env miss, and no probe produced a miss.",
      "PLANNING READ (2026-11-27, main 7405236dba6, plan-file gate over the live authority by calm-hawk-32): THE TWO RECEIPTS ABOVE MEASURE DIFFERENT TREES AND ARE LEFT IN CONFLICT ON PURPOSE - neither is edited or deleted here, so a reader still sees the disagreement. WHICH READS WHICH TREE: the repair receipt reads the PRE-REPAIR failing state under the namespace-only name-resolution policy, as its own text says (the reading is on the failing call, before the census gate yielded on import_visible_name); the CURRENT RUNG receipt of 2026-11-23 at main 4a63370f4a67 reads the POST-REPAIR tree and is the current standing of this class. WHAT IS STILL NOT SHOWN, and is not showable without one instrumentation read inside call_target_for_direct_call, is that any CURRENT corpus call actually misses func_env: the census answer for a listed-imported method-template name is reachable only on a func_env miss; func_env parents are built from the module's listed imports at BOTH sites (func_env_views_for_import defined src/v1/04_infer.dag:20860, called at :21059 in build_module_context and at :23498 in rewire_func_env_parent_links); and import_visible_name reads a DIFFERENT authority, type_env.source_visible_names at src/v1/04_env.dag:784, mirrored by the gates at src/v1/04_lookup.dag:332 and :753 - so func-env membership and import-visibility membership cannot be assumed to agree, and the pair stays unresolved until that instrument is read. CITATION FIXED, measured: the bare call is skip(xs: ws, n: 1) at dag/gunbc/fleet/fleet_known_hosts_anchor.dag:983, inside fn portable_remote_words at :969, not at :767 as the first receipt cites - that file has exactly two skip( sites, :983 and :1038 (inside fn login_shell_standing at :1023), and line 767 is a lone closing brace; the target is fn skip<T>(xs: FreeMonoid<T>, n: Int) at dag/std/algebra.dag:1364 and the listed import is import std.algebra { trim, list_head, skip } at :10. THE WITNESS THIS CLASS'S REMOVABILITY WAS ARGUED FROM NO L